EXAM_DATA.papers["2001"] = {"id":"2001","year":2001,"label":"2001 旧卷","era":"old","sourceUrl":"https://english-exam.lazynote.cn/kaoyan/paper/2001/","timeLimitMin":180,"scoreMode":"raw","parts":[{"id":"section1","kind":"cloze","title":"Section I 完形填空","directions":"Directions: For each numbered blank in the following passage, there are four choices marked [A], [B], [C] and [D]. Choose the best one and mark your answer on ANSWER SHEET 1 by blackening the corresponding letter in the brackets with a pencil. (10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section1-1","text":"The government is to ban payments to witnesses by newspapers seeking to buy up people involved in prominent cases   {{1}}   the trial of Rosemary West."},{"id":"p-section1-2","text":"In a significant   {{2}}   of legal controls over the press, Lord Irvine, the Lord Chancellor, will introduce a   {{3}}   bill that will propose making payments to witnesses   {{4}}   and will strictly control the amount of   {{5}}   that can be given to a case   {{6}}   a trial begins."},{"id":"p-section1-3","text":"In a letter to Gerald Kaufman, chairman of the House of Commons media select committee, Lord Irvine said he   {{7}}   with a committee report this year which said that self regulation did not   {{8}}   sufficient control."},{"id":"p-section1-4","text":"{{9}}   of the letter came two days after Lord Irvine caused a   {{10}}   of media protest when he said the   {{11}}   of privacy controls contained in European legislation would be left to judges   {{12}}   to Parliament."},{"id":"p-section1-5","text":"The Lord Chancellor said introduction of the Human Rights Bill, which   {{13}}   the European Convention on Human Rights legally   {{14}}   in Britain, laid down that everybody was   {{15}}   to privacy and that public figures could go to court to protect themselves and their families."},{"id":"p-section1-6","text":"\"Press freedoms will be in safe hands   {{16}}   our British judges,\" he said."},{"id":"p-section1-7","text":"Witness payments became an   {{17}}   after West was sentenced to 10 life sentences in 1995. Up to 19 witnesses were   {{18}}   to have received payments for telling their stories to newspapers. Concerns were raised   {{19}}   witnesses might be encouraged to exaggerate their stories in court to   {{20}}   guilty verdicts."}]},"questions":[{"n":1,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"as to"},{"key":"B","text":"for instance"},{"key":"C","text":"in particular"},{"key":"D","text":"such as"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"1.","reason":"上义复数名词后直接接单个例子 线索就在本句内：prominent cases __(1)__ the trial of Rosemary West——cases 是上义、复数；后面是单个具体案例。能直接\"上义 + ___ + 例子\"且语法不出错的连接成分才合规。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"as to 相当于 about/regarding，引出的是\"涉及的话题\"，不是\"举一个例子\"。说 prominent cases as to the trial of...，逻辑变成\"关于该审判的著名案件\"，与原文\"举例说明何为著名案件\"南辕北辙。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"for instance 语义上对，但句法不对：它通常作插入语，前后要用逗号或句号断开（cases, for instance, the trial of...），而原文是连写、无标点。考研一完形常用这类\"语义对但句法不合\"的项做陷阱，识破它是关键。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"in particular 是\"特别地、尤其\"，常后置修饰前面的名词（cases in particular）或作插入语，并不能直接带出一个名词短语充当具体例子。结构上也跟 for instance 一样需要标点支持。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"such as 是\"诸如\"，最典型用法就是 N + such as + 具体例子，且不需要逗号断开，完美匹配 prominent cases __(1)__ the trial of Rosemary West 的句法框架，语义也准确（\"诸如 West 案这类著名案件\"）。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":2,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"tightening"},{"key":"B","text":"intensifying"},{"key":"C","text":"focusing"},{"key":"D","text":"fastening"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"2.","reason":"中心词 controls 决定搭配 线索是空后的中心词：__(2)__ of legal controls over the press，再结合下一行 will strictly control the amount of __(5)__ 的 strictly control 呼应——可知政府是在\"收紧\"对媒体的管控。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"tighten controls/regulations 是英语新闻里\"收紧管控\"的固定说法，与 strictly control 同向呼应，完美贴合\"政府加强法律管控\"的语境。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"intensifying 意为\"加剧、强化\"，常搭 efforts/competition/attacks，强调\"程度加深\"。与 controls 搭配生硬，且 intensify 多用于负面或强烈活动的加剧，不是\"立法加强管控\"的惯用搭配。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"focusing 是\"集中、聚焦于某点\"，不含\"加强\"之意。后面也会接 on，而原文是 of，不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"fastening 指\"系紧、扣紧\"（系扣安全带、拉链），是物理动作，不用于抽象的法律管控。属于形近义错的干扰项。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":3,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sketch"},{"key":"B","text":"rough"},{"key":"C","text":"preliminary"},{"key":"D","text":"draft"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"3.","reason":"中心词是法律意义的 bill 空后 will introduce a __(3)__ bill 中的 bill 在英国政治语境里是\"议案/法案\"。法律文本里的\"草案\"有固定说法。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"sketch 是\"草图、速写、梗概\"，多见于绘画、写作大纲，与 bill 不搭，常听\"sketch a plan\"，但不说 sketch bill。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"rough 作形容词指\"粗糙的、粗略的\"，rough draft 才常用；单独 rough bill 不是地道搭配。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"preliminary 表\"初步的、预备的\"（preliminary report/study），强调\"先于正式阶段\"。立法语境里说\"草案\"用 draft bill，不用 preliminary bill。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"draft 是法律/立法语境里\"草案\"的标准词，draft bill 就是\"法案草案\"的固定说法，与 introduce 这一立法动作严丝合缝。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":4,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"illogical"},{"key":"B","text":"illegal"},{"key":"C","text":"improbable"},{"key":"D","text":"improper"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"4.","reason":"立法 bill 直接的目的 线索在前后：will introduce a __(3)__ bill that will propose making payments to witnesses __(4)__——一份法案最直接能让某行为变成的状态是\"非法\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"illogical 是\"不合逻辑的\"，立法管不到\"逻辑\"，不可能通过一部法案让某事变得 illogical。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"illegal 是\"非法的\"，恰是 ban 在法律语义上的目的——通过法案把\"付钱给证人\"宣告为非法。与第 1 段 ban payments to witnesses 完全对应。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"improbable 是\"不太可能发生的\"，是概率/可能性评价，立法可降低发生概率，但不能直接把行为\"变成不可能\"——表达不到位。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"improper 是\"不当的、不合适的\"，多为道德/礼节评价。立法要做的不是\"宣告不当\"而是\"宣告违法\"，比 illegal 弱一档。考研一常用\"语义偏弱\"的项做诱饵。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":5,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"publicity"},{"key":"B","text":"penalty"},{"key":"C","text":"popularity"},{"key":"D","text":"peculiarity"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"5.","reason":"媒体在审前对案件的报道量 线索在本句与前句：第 1 段说政府针对的是\"报纸\"（by newspapers），第 2 段又说\"严格控制审前给一个案件 ___ 的量\"（will strictly control the amount of __(5)__ that can be given to a case __(6)__ a trial begins）。报纸+案件+审前+量——只有\"报道/曝光度\"语义上才说得通。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"publicity 指\"公众关注/媒体曝光/宣传\"，正是\"报纸在审前给一个案件多少报道量\"的精确表达，与全文媒体话题一脉相承。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"penalty 是\"处罚、罚金\"。\"审前给案件多少处罚\"逻辑不通——刑罚是判决后才有，且来源不是报纸。属于形近义错。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"popularity 是\"受欢迎度\"，是中性偏褒，用于人物或产品。刑事案件不会有\"受欢迎度\"。考研一常用这种色彩失配的形近词诱骗。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"peculiarity 是\"独特性、怪癖\"，与媒体审前报道毫无逻辑关系。形近迷惑而已。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":6,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"since"},{"key":"B","text":"if"},{"key":"C","text":"before"},{"key":"D","text":"as"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"逻辑关系","stemZh":"6.","reason":"管控针对的是审判开始之前 线索就在本句：control the amount of __(5)__ that can be given to a case __(6)__ a trial begins——立法管控的是\"庭审尚未开始\"那个阶段的媒体曝光，避免影响审判。完全是\"在审判开始之前\"的时间关系。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"since 引导时间状语指\"从那时起\"（庭审开始后到现在），与\"庭审尚未开始\"相反。属于时间方向错。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"if 是\"如果\"，把\"庭审开始\"说成假设条件，但已经预设要立案审理，\"开始庭审\"是必然事件，不是 if 关系。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"before 直接表达\"庭审开始之前\"这个时间段，与\"避免审前媒体过度曝光影响审判\"的立法初衷严丝合缝。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"as 作时间连词是\"在……期间/正当……时\"，意味管控发生在审判进行时，与\"审前\"语义不符。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":7,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sided"},{"key":"B","text":"shared"},{"key":"C","text":"complied"},{"key":"D","text":"agreed"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"7.","reason":"和委员会报告（意见）的关系 线索在本句：he __(7)__ with a committee report this year which said that self regulation did not __(8)__ sufficient control. 大法官表达对一份报告\"观点\"的态度——是赞同。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"sided with 表\"站在某人/某方一边\"（side with sb），宾语必须是人或党派，不接\"报告\"。考研一常用\"语义半对、搭配宾语错\"的项做迷惑。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"shared 表\"分享/共有（观点）\"时，宾语直接是 view/opinion（share the view），不是 share with a report。结构错。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"complied with 表\"遵守、服从\"（comply with the rule/order），宾语应是规则、命令、法律。这里只是\"赞同报告的观点\"，不是\"服从一份报告\"。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"agreed with 后接观点、看法、报告，表\"同意（其中观点）\"，语义和搭配双对——与后文 said 引出报告观点完全吻合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":8,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"present"},{"key":"B","text":"offer"},{"key":"C","text":"manifest"},{"key":"D","text":"indicate"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"8.","reason":"自律是否能\"提供\"足够管控 线索在本句：self regulation did not __(8)__ sufficient control，主语是\"自律\"，宾语是\"足够的管控\"。语义关系是\"自律提供/给予 管控\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"present 是\"呈现、展示、提交\"，宾语多为 report/idea/gift。说 present control 不成立——管控不是被\"展示\"的东西。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"offer 是\"提供\"，宾语可为 help/support/protection/control 等\"可被给予的东西\"，offer sufficient control 即\"提供足够的管控\"，自然贴切。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"manifest 是\"显示出（症状、迹象）\"，宾语多为 symptoms/signs/feelings。manifest control 在英语里几乎不出现。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"indicate 是\"表明、暗示\"，宾语为信息/迹象（indicate a problem）。说\"自律不能 indicate sufficient control\"逻辑跳脱——报告说的是自律没\"做到\"足够管控，而非\"没暗示\"。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":9,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Release"},{"key":"B","text":"Publication"},{"key":"C","text":"Printing"},{"key":"D","text":"Exposure"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"9.","reason":"宾语是 letter（公开信） 线索是本句中心词：__(9)__ of the letter 中 letter 是\"信函\"。信函在媒体语境里通常是\"刊登/公开发表\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"Release 偏\"发布、发行、释放\"，常用 release of news/film/prisoner。信函更常用 publication。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"Publication 表\"出版、公开发表\"，正是公开信/书面意见对外披露的标准词，publication of the letter 在新闻英语里是固定说法。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"Printing 指\"印刷\"这一物理过程，本文要表达的是\"信被公开\"，重点不在印刷工艺。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"Exposure 是\"曝光、揭露\"，含\"原本不愿公开却被掀出\"的色彩，与大法官\"主动写信表态\"的语境矛盾。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":10,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"storm"},{"key":"B","text":"rage"},{"key":"C","text":"flare"},{"key":"D","text":"flash"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"10.","reason":"媒体大规模抗议的隐喻 线索就在本句：caused a __(10)__ of media protest——\"引发了一场媒体抗议的 ___\"，需要一个能比喻\"大面积爆发的舆论反应\"的词。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"storm 在新闻英语里是表\"大规模强烈舆论反应\"的常用比喻，a storm of protest/criticism/controversy 都是固定搭配，符合\"引发媒体抗议的风暴\"的语义。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"rage 是\"暴怒\"，自身已是情绪名词，不说 a rage of protest——同义重复不自然。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"flare 指\"闪光/突然燃起\"，多用于 a flare of temper/anger（指个人怒气一闪），不用于\"大范围媒体抗议\"。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"flash 是\"闪光、瞬间\"，强调短暂；媒体抗议是持续性事件，不用 flash 比喻。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":11,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"translation"},{"key":"B","text":"interpretation"},{"key":"C","text":"exhibition"},{"key":"D","text":"demonstration"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"11.","reason":"对法律条款的解读 线索：__(11)__ of privacy controls contained in European legislation would be left to judges __(12)__ to Parliament——是对欧洲立法里隐私条款的\"解读\"，且这一权力交给法官、而非议会。法官对法律的工作是\"解释\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"translation 是\"语际翻译\"，跨语言转换。法官的工作不是把欧盟文本翻成英语，而是裁定其含义。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"interpretation 是\"解释、释义\"，interpretation of law 是法学固定术语，指法官对成文法条文的释义裁定。与 judges 搭配天衣无缝。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"exhibition 指\"展览\"，常用于艺术品、产品。法律条款不会被\"展览\"。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"demonstration 是\"演示、示威\"，演示用于产品/原理，示威用于政治运动，都跟\"解读法律\"无关。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":12,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"better than"},{"key":"B","text":"other than"},{"key":"C","text":"rather than"},{"key":"D","text":"sooner than"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"12.","reason":"解释权交给法官而非议会 线索：would be left to judges __(12)__ to Parliament——把解释权交给\"法官\"而不是\"议会\"，是\"选 A 而非 B\"的取舍关系。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"better than 是\"比……更好\"，强调程度比较；本文不是说法官\"比议会更好\"，而是\"选法官、不选议会\"的取舍，定性错。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"other than 表\"除了……之外\"或\"不同于\"，常用于排除/区别（no one other than him）。这里说的不是\"除议会之外\"，而是直接的二选一。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"rather than 是\"而不是\"，正是\"选法官、不选议会\"的取舍语义，对应大法官明示的立场偏好。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"sooner than 字面\"比……更早\"，引申\"宁愿……也不\"，用在\"sooner than do, I would die\"这种句式。这里没有时间或宁愿语义。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":13,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"changes"},{"key":"B","text":"makes"},{"key":"C","text":"sets"},{"key":"D","text":"turns"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"13.","reason":"宾补结构 make sth + adj 线索是本句的句法骨架：__(13)__ the European Convention on Human Rights legally __(14)__——动词后是名词宾语，再后是形容词补足语。能容下这个 \"宾 + adj\" 结构、且与\"使条约在英国法律上有约束力\"语义吻合的，是 make。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"changes 后面不能直接跟 \"宾 + adj\" 结构；要表\"使变成……\"得用 change ... into ...，与原文句法不符。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"makes 完美适配\"make + 宾 + adj\"使役结构，make sth legally binding 是法律英语固定说法（\"使……具有法律约束力\"），与 __(14)__ 的 binding 强强联动。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"sets 后跟形容词需特定搭配（set sb free），不能随意 set sth legally binding；句法不通。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"turns 表\"变\"需 turn into 或 turn + adj（如 turn red）形态变化，且 turn 多用于自身变化，不用于\"使法律文件具有约束力\"。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":14,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"binding"},{"key":"B","text":"convincing"},{"key":"C","text":"restraining"},{"key":"D","text":"sustaining"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"14.","reason":"法案使公约具有法律约束力 线索：which __(13)__ the European Convention on Human Rights legally __(14)__ in Britain——人权法案的作用是让欧洲人权公约在英国\"具有法律效力\"。法律语义只能是\"binding\"。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"binding 与 legally 搭配是法律英语固定术语，意为\"具有法律约束力的\"，恰好表达\"使欧洲人权公约在英国具有法律效力\"。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"convincing 是\"令人信服的\"，常修饰 argument/evidence。\"使法律 convincing\"不通——法律不是因说服力起作用。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"restraining 是\"限制、约束\"（restraining order 限制令），有\"压制\"色彩，且不与 legally 形成法律术语。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"sustaining 是\"维持、支撑\"，多与生命/努力/经济搭，与\"法律约束力\"无关。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":15,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"authorized"},{"key":"B","text":"credited"},{"key":"C","text":"entitled"},{"key":"D","text":"qualified"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"15.","reason":"人人享有隐私权 线索：everybody was __(15)__ to privacy and that public figures could go to court to protect themselves——\"人人有权享有隐私\"，紧跟 \"公众人物可上法庭保护自己\"，正是权利主张的语义。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"authorized to do 表\"被授权做某事\"，多用于职务授权（authorized to sign）；不与 to privacy 这种\"享有某物\"的语义搭配。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"credited with 表\"被归功于\"，credited with sth；用 to 不是它的固定搭配，且与\"享有权利\"语义偏离。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"entitled to (sth) 是\"有权获得/享有\"的标准搭配，be entitled to privacy 即\"享有隐私权\"，与法律文本表达完全一致。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"qualified for/to do 表\"具备资格、合格\"（qualified for the job），更侧重\"达到条件\"，而非\"享有权利\"。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":16,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"with"},{"key":"B","text":"to"},{"key":"C","text":"from"},{"key":"D","text":"by"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"固定搭配","stemZh":"16.","reason":"press freedoms 在 judges 手里安全 线索：Press freedoms will be in safe hands __(16)__ our British judges——\"新闻自由在我们英国法官那里是安全的\"。\"在某人手中\"的英语标准说法是 with sb。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"with 与 hands 形成 in safe hands with sb 的固定结构，表\"由某人掌管很安心\"，正好契合\"信任英国法官\"的语义。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"to 表\"朝向/给到\"，in safe hands to sb 不是地道用法；hand sth to sb 用 to，但这里是 in hands 结构。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"from 表\"来源\"，in safe hands from sb 没有这种搭配；且与\"由谁掌管\"的语义相反。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"by 引出动作执行者（被动语态），但 in safe hands 已是状态短语，无需 by 引执行者。be in safe hands by sb 不是英语习惯。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":17,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"impact"},{"key":"B","text":"incident"},{"key":"C","text":"inference"},{"key":"D","text":"issue"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"17.","reason":"证人付费成为公共争议焦点 线索：Witness payments became an __(17)__ after West was sentenced to 10 life sentences in 1995——证人付费在 1995 年 West 被判后成为社会讨论的\"议题/争议\"，是公共政策性问题。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"impact 是\"影响、冲击\"，常 have/make an impact on，不说\"X 成为一个 impact\"。语义和搭配都偏。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"incident 指\"单一事件/事故\"，是发生过的具体事，不是话题。\"付费现象\"是反复出现的实践，不是一次性 incident。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"inference 是\"推断、推论\"，思维过程或结论，与\"成为社会议题\"完全不沾边。属形近义错。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"issue 是\"议题、争议\"，在公共讨论语境里是标配，become an issue 表\"成为一个公共议题\"，与本段交代立法背景的功能贴合。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":18,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"stated"},{"key":"B","text":"remarked"},{"key":"C","text":"said"},{"key":"D","text":"told"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"语法形态","stemZh":"18.","reason":"句型 be said to have done 线索是句法结构本身：Up to 19 witnesses were __(18)__ to have received payments——\"据说多达 19 名证人收过钱\"，正是 \"It is said that...\" / \"sb is said to do\" 的句型。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"stated 后多接 that 从句（state that...）或直接宾语，be stated to have done 极少用，不是地道句型。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"remarked 后跟 on sth 或 that 从句，be remarked to have done 不通行。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"said 嵌入 \"be said to do/have done\" 是英语固定句型，表\"据说\"。本句即\"据说多达 19 名证人收过钱\"——与后文 Concerns were raised 的传闻基调相承。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"told 是双宾动词（tell sb sth），其被动语态 be told 后接 sth 或 to do（被告诉做某事）——\"19 名证人被告诉收过钱\"逻辑荒谬。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":19,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"what"},{"key":"B","text":"when"},{"key":"C","text":"which"},{"key":"D","text":"that"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"语法形态","stemZh":"19.","reason":"concerns 的同位语从句 线索：Concerns were raised __(19)__ witnesses might be encouraged to exaggerate their stories in court——后接的从句结构完整（主谓宾齐备），不缺成分；语义上是对\"concerns\"具体内容的解释，是典型的同位语从句。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"what 引导从句时必充当从句成分（主/宾/表），而本从句结构完整不缺。语法上行不通。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"when 引导时间状语，但 concerns were raised when... 表\"在……时担忧被提起\"，逻辑变成时间从句，而原文是对担忧内容的解释。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"which 作关系代词须在从句里充当主/宾；这里从句结构完整不缺成分，且 which 引导限制性定语从句时一般紧贴先行词（concerns 与 which 之间隔了 were raised，更不像定语从句）。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"that 引导同位语从句，解释 concerns 的具体内容（即\"证人可能被怂恿夸大证词\"）。语法和语义双对，是抽象名词后同位语的标配。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}},{"n":20,"stem":"","options":[{"key":"A","text":"assure"},{"key":"B","text":"confide"},{"key":"C","text":"ensure"},{"key":"D","text":"guarantee"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义辨析","stemZh":"20.","reason":"宾语是结果，确保结果发生 线索：exaggerate their stories in court to __(20)__ guilty verdicts——证人在庭上夸大证词的目的是\"确保产生有罪判决\"。宾语是结果（verdicts），不是人。","options":{"A":{"mark":"","note":"assure 意为\"使人放心、向某人保证\"，标准搭配是 assure sb (of sth) / assure sb that...，宾语必须是人。本句宾语是 verdicts（结果），不合搭配。考研一最高频的近义干扰。"},"B":{"mark":"","note":"confide 是\"吐露秘密、信任地告诉\"（confide in sb；confide sth to sb），与\"确保结果\"语义完全无关。"},"C":{"mark":"","note":"ensure 是\"确保某事发生\"，宾语是事（结果、行为），ensure guilty verdicts 即\"确保得到有罪判决\"，与\"夸大证词以获定罪\"的逻辑严密对应。"},"D":{"mark":"","note":"guarantee 也可表\"保证\"，但更常用于商业/正式承诺（guarantee the quality），且语气是\"许诺一定如此\"——证人靠夸大证词不能 guarantee 法官的判决，语用偏差。"}},"choiceEn":"","clues":[]}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-1","kind":"reading","title":"Text 1","textNo":1,"directions":"Directions: Each of the passages below is followed by some questions. For each questions there are four answers marked [A], [B], [C] and [D]. Read the passages carefully and choose the best answer to each of the questions. Then mark your answer on ANSWER SHEET 1 by blackening the corresponding letter in the brackets with a pencil. (40 points)","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 1","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-1","text":"Specialisation can be seen as a response to the problem of an increasing accumulation of scientific knowledge. By splitting up the subject matter into smaller units, one man could continue to handle the information and use it as the basis for further research. But specialisation was only one of a series of related developments in science affecting the process of communication. Another was the growing professionalisation of scientific activity."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-2","text":"No clear-cut distinction can be drawn between professionals and amateurs in science: exceptions can be found to any rule. Nevertheless, the word \"amateur\" does carry a connotation that the person concerned is not fully integrated into the scientific community and, in particular, may not fully share its values. The growth of specialisation in the nineteenth century, with its consequent requirement of a longer, more complex training, implied greater problems for amateur participation in science. The trend was naturally most obvious in those areas of science based especially on a mathematical or laboratory training, and can be illustrated in terms of the development of geology in the United Kingdom."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-3","text":"A comparison of British geological publications over the last century and a half reveals not simply an increasing emphasis on the primacy of research, but also a changing definition of what constitutes an acceptable research paper. Thus, in the nineteenth century, local geological studies represented worthwhile research in their own right; but, in the twentieth century, local studies have increasingly become acceptable to professionals only if they incorporate, and reflect on, the wider geological picture. Amateurs, on the other hand, have continued to pursue local studies in the old way. The overall result has been to make entrance to professional geological journals harder for amateurs, a result that has been reinforced by the widespread introduction of refereeing, first by national journals in the nineteenth century and then by several local geological journals in the twentieth century. As a logical consequence of this development, separate journals have now appeared aimed mainly towards either professional or amateur readership. A rather similar process of differentiation has led to professional geologists coming together nationally within one or two specific societies, whereas the amateurs have tended either to remain in local societies or to come together nationally in a different way."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-1-4","text":"Although the process of professionalisation and specialisation was already well under way in British geology during the nineteenth century, its full consequences were thus delayed until the twentieth century. In science generally, however, the nineteenth century must be reckoned as the crucial period for this change in the structure of science."}]},"questions":[{"n":21,"stem":"The growth of specialisation in the 19th century might be more clearly seen in sciences such as____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"sociology and chemistry"},{"key":"B","text":"physics and psychology"},{"key":"C","text":"sociology and psychology"},{"key":"D","text":"physics and chemistry"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"19世纪专业化的发展在诸如____等科学领域可能表现得更为明显","choicesZh":{"A":"社会学和化学","B":"物理学和心理学","C":"社会学和心理学","D":"物理学和化学"},"analysis":{"type":"might be more clearly seen in sciences such as____ 问的是「可以在哪些具体学科中更清晰看到」，答案必须是文中点名的学科，而不是推断的结论。","parse":"The growth of specialisation in the 19th century might be more clearly seen in sciences such as____.：主语是 The growth of specialisation in the 19th century，谓语是 might be more clearly seen，介词短语 in sciences such as ____ 充当地点状语，空格处需要填入若干具体学科名。无陷阱。","locateEn":"The trend was naturally most obvious in those areas of science based especially on a mathematical or laboratory training, and can be illustrated in terms of the development of geology in the United Kingdom.","locateZh":"这种趋势自然在那些尤其依赖数学训练或实验训练的科学领域最为明显，并可以通过英国地质学的发展加以说明。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"sociology and chemistry 中 chemistry 符合「实验训练」，但 sociology（社会学）以社会调查与思辨为主，并不以 a mathematical or laboratory training 为根基。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"physics and psychology 中 physics 符合，但 psychology 当时并非以数学或实验为核心训练，与原文 based especially on a mathematical or laboratory training 的「especially」语气不符。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"sociology and psychology 中 sociology 与 psychology 都不以 a mathematical or laboratory training 为基础，与定位句完全不匹配。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判要求「数学训练+实验训练」型学科，physics and chemistry 中物理对应数学训练、化学对应实验训练，是四个选项里唯一双特征均满足的组合，自然锁定 D。","pairs":[{"orig":"based especially on a mathematical or laboratory training","opt":"physics and chemistry"}]}}}}},{"n":22,"stem":"We can infer from the passage that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"there is little distinction between specialisation and professionalisation"},{"key":"B","text":"amateurs can compete with professionals in some areas of science"},{"key":"C","text":"professionals tend to welcome amateurs into the scientific community"},{"key":"D","text":"amateurs have national academic societies but no local ones"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从文章中我们可以推断出____","choicesZh":{"A":"专业化与职业化之间几乎没有区别","B":"业余爱好者可以在某些科学领域与专业人士竞争","C":"专业人士倾向于欢迎业余爱好者进入科学界","D":"业余爱好者有全国性的学术团体但没有地方性的"},"analysis":{"type":"We can infer from the passage that____. 没有给任何具体话题，只用 infer 标明题型——答案是原文事实的「一步逻辑延伸」。","parse":"We can infer from the passage that____.：主语 We，谓语 can infer，from the passage 是状语，that 引导宾语从句，空格处就是要填入的从句内容。结构平铺，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Thus, in the nineteenth century, local geological studies represented worthwhile research in their own right; but, in the twentieth century, local studies have increasingly become acceptable to professionals only if they incorporate, and reflect on, the wider geological picture. Amateurs, on the other hand, have continued to pursue local studies in the old way.","locateZh":"因此，在十九世纪，地方性的地质研究本身就是有价值的研究；但到了二十世纪，地方性研究只有在纳入并思考更宏观的地质背景时，才日益被专业人士认可。而业余爱好者则仍以旧方式继续从事地方性研究。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"there is little distinction between specialisation and professionalisation 与原文 But specialisation was only one of a series of related developments in science affecting the process of communication. Another was the growing professionalisation of scientific activity. 相悖：原文明确把二者作为两个相关但独立的发展趋势并列展开。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"amateurs can compete with professionals in some areas of science 的限定词「some areas」与「exceptions」对应严丝合缝，强度恰好——不是「全部领域」、也不是「无法竞争」，正是推断题最稳妥的「中等强度」选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"exceptions can be found to any rule","opt":"amateurs can compete with professionals in some areas of science"},{"orig":"No clear-cut distinction can be drawn between professionals and amateurs in science","opt":"amateurs can compete with professionals in some areas of science"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"professionals tend to welcome amateurs into the scientific community 在原文找不到任何对应；恰相反，The overall result has been to make entrance to professional geological journals harder for amateurs 显示专业者反而在抬高门槛。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"amateurs have national academic societies but no local ones 与 the amateurs have tended either to remain in local societies or to come together nationally in a different way 相悖：原文恰恰说业余者既留在地方性团体中、也以另一种方式在全国层面集结。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":23,"stem":"The author writes of the development of geology to demonstrate____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the process of specialisation and professionalisation"},{"key":"B","text":"the hardship of amateurs in scientific study"},{"key":"C","text":"the change of policies in scientific publications"},{"key":"D","text":"the discrimination of professionals against amateurs"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"作者论述地质学的发展是为了说明____","choicesZh":{"A":"专业化与职业化的过程","B":"业余爱好者在科学研究中的艰辛","C":"科学出版物政策的变化","D":"专业人士对业余爱好者的歧视"},"analysis":{"type":"The author writes of the development of geology to demonstrate____. 直接用 to demonstrate 提问「写 geology 是为了证明什么」，是典型的例证目的题。","parse":"The author writes of the development of geology to demonstrate____.：主语 The author，谓语 writes of，宾语 the development of geology，不定式 to demonstrate 表目的，空格处填作者写它的真正目的。无陷阱。","locateEn":"A comparison of British geological publications over the last century and a half reveals not simply an increasing emphasis on the primacy of research, but also a changing definition of what constitutes an acceptable research paper.","locateZh":"对过去一个半世纪英国地质学出版物的比较所揭示的，不仅是研究的至高地位日益受到强调，还有「什么算得上一篇可接受的研究论文」的定义也在变化。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"the process of specialisation and professionalisation 是 geology 例证所服务的上位论点的标准名词化表达，与定位句的论点完全对齐，故为正确答案。","pairs":[{"orig":"The growth of specialisation in the nineteenth century, with its consequent requirement of a longer, more complex training, implied greater problems for amateur participation in science.","opt":"the process of specialisation and professionalisation"},{"orig":"Another was the growing professionalisation of scientific activity.","opt":"the process of specialisation and professionalisation"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the hardship of amateurs in scientific study 只是 implied greater problems for amateur participation in science 论点的后果之一，是例证内部的具体细节，并非作者写 geology 的主旨意图。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"the change of policies in scientific publications 对应 reinforced by the widespread introduction of refereeing 等细节，是 geology 例证内部用以呈现专业化的现象，而非作者写 geology 想说明的真正目的。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the discrimination of professionals against amateurs 把原文中「门槛提高」「分流出版」「分别组建团体」描述为带有道德判断的 discrimination（歧视），而原文用的都是中性叙述词。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":24,"stem":"The direct reason for specialisation is____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the development in communication"},{"key":"B","text":"the growth of professionalisation"},{"key":"C","text":"the expansion of scientific knowledge"},{"key":"D","text":"the splitting up of academic societies"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"专业化的直接原因是____","choicesZh":{"A":"通信技术的发展","B":"职业化的发展","C":"科学知识的扩展","D":"学术团体的分裂"},"analysis":{"type":"The direct reason for specialisation is____. 问的是 specialisation 的直接原因，原文必有对应的因果句，属于细节题中的因果细节。","parse":"The direct reason for specialisation is____.：主语 The direct reason，介词短语 for specialisation 修饰主语，系动词 is，表语空格。形容词 direct 是题眼，决定排除「间接因」。","locateEn":"Specialisation can be seen as a response to the problem of an increasing accumulation of scientific knowledge.","locateZh":"专业化可以被视为对科学知识不断累积这一问题的一种应对。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"the development in communication 对应原文 But specialisation was only one of a series of related developments in science affecting the process of communication.，专业化与「沟通过程」是「同列相关变化」而非「因果关系」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"the growth of professionalisation 对应原文 Another was the growing professionalisation of scientific activity.——职业化是与专业化同列的「另一相关发展」，而非专业化的直接原因。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"the expansion of scientific knowledge 直接对应定位句中作为 response 对象的那个名词短语，是四个选项里唯一保留「科学知识本身在变多」这一核心因果指向的选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"an increasing accumulation of scientific knowledge","opt":"the expansion of scientific knowledge"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the splitting up of academic societies 对应原文 professional geologists coming together nationally within one or two specific societies, whereas the amateurs have tended either to remain in local societies or to come together nationally in a different way，那是专业化推进后造成的结果，因果方向被颠倒。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-2","kind":"reading","title":"Text 2","textNo":2,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 2","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-1","text":"A great deal of attention is being paid today to the so-called digital divide—the division of the world into the info (information) rich and the info poor. And that divide does exist today. My wife and I lectured about this looming danger twenty years ago. What was less visible then, however, were the new, positive forces that work against the digital divide. There are reasons to be optimistic."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-2","text":"There are technological reasons to hope the digital divide will narrow. As the Internet becomes more and more commercialized, it is in the interest of business to universalize access—after all, the more people online, the more potential customers there are. More and more governments, afraid their countries will be left behind, want to spread Internet access. Within the next decade or two, one to two billion people on the planet will be netted together. As a result, I now believe the digital divide will narrow rather than widen in the years ahead. And that is very good news because the Internet may well be the most powerful tool for combating world poverty that we've ever had."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-3","text":"Of course, the use of the Internet isn't the only way to defeat poverty. And the Internet is not the only tool we have. But it has enormous potential."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-2-4","text":"To take advantage of this tool, some impoverished countries will have to get over their outdated anti-colonial prejudices with respect to foreign investment. Countries that still think foreign investment is an invasion of their sovereignty might well study the history of infrastructure (the basic structural foundations of a society) in the United States. When the United States built its industrial infrastructure, it didn't have the capital to do so. And that is why America's Second Wave infrastructure—including roads, harbors, highways, ports and so on—was built with foreign investment. The English, the Germans, the Dutch and the French were investing in Britain's former colony. They financed them. Immigrant Americans built them. Guess who owns them now? The Americans. I believe the same thing would be true in places like Brazil or anywhere else for that matter. The more foreign capital you have helping you build your Third Wave infrastructure, which today is an electronic infrastructure, the better off you're going to be. That doesn't mean lying down and becoming fooled, or letting foreign corporations run uncontrolled. But it does mean recognizing how important they can be in building the energy and telecom infrastructures needed to take full advantage of the Internet."}]},"questions":[{"n":25,"stem":"Digital divide is something____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"getting worse because of the Internet"},{"key":"B","text":"the rich countries are responsible for"},{"key":"C","text":"the world must guard against"},{"key":"D","text":"considered positive today"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"数字鸿沟是____的东西。","choicesZh":{"A":"因互联网而变得更加严重","B":"富裕国家应当为之负责","C":"世界必须加以防范","D":"如今被认为是积极的"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Digital divide is something____ 是把 digital divide 这个话题词补完性质，问的是文中对它的客观定性，属于细节性质判断。","parse":"Digital divide is something____ 是一个待补全的判断句，主语是话题词 digital divide，系动词 is 后接 something + 形容词性后置修饰（选项补出）。结构平铺直叙，无陷阱，关键是看清选项是在补 something 的修饰语。","locateEn":"And that divide does exist today. ... What was less visible then, however, were the new, positive forces that work against the digital divide.","locateZh":"那种鸿沟在今天确实存在……不过当时不太能看到的，是那些正在抵抗数字鸿沟的、新的、积极的力量。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文将互联网视为对抗鸿沟、对抗贫困的力量（the most powerful tool for combating world poverty），而 getting worse because of the Internet 把互联网说成是鸿沟恶化的元凶，与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说存在 info rich 与 info poor 的划分（the division of the world into the info (information) rich and the info poor），并未追究\"鸿沟由富国造成\"这一责任归属，the rich countries are responsible for 系无中生有。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判结论\"客观存在且需警惕\"与 the world must guard against 完全对应：guard against 正是 looming danger 的应对动作，没有任何信息越界。","pairs":[{"orig":"looming danger","opt":"the world must guard against"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文称鸿沟为 looming danger，态度明显负面；considered positive today 反把鸿沟定性为\"被视为积极的事\"，与作者立场相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":26,"stem":"Governments attach importance to the Internet because it____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"offers economic potentials"},{"key":"B","text":"can bring foreign funds"},{"key":"C","text":"can soon wipe out world poverty"},{"key":"D","text":"connects people all over the world"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"各国政府重视互联网是因为它____。","choicesZh":{"A":"提供经济潜力","B":"能够带来外国资金","C":"能够很快消除世界贫困","D":"连接世界各地的人们"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Governments attach importance to the Internet because it____ 用 because 直接索取原文给出的理由，是对原文细节的同义替换提问。","parse":"Governments attach importance to the Internet because it____ 主句 Governments attach importance to the Internet 已给出态度，because 引导原因状语从句，主语 it 指代 the Internet。选项补的就是 it 后的谓语部分，结构清晰、无陷阱。","locateEn":"As the Internet becomes more and more commercialized, it is in the interest of business to universalize access—after all, the more people online, the more potential customers there are. More and more governments, afraid their countries will be left behind, want to spread Internet access.","locateZh":"随着互联网越来越商业化，普及上网是合乎商业利益的——毕竟，上网人越多，潜在客户就越多。越来越多的政府，因为担心本国掉队，希望扩大互联网接入。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"预判已锁\"经济动机\"，offers economic potentials 一一对应原文 business + potential customers，无任何越界。","pairs":[{"orig":"it is in the interest of business to universalize access","opt":"offers economic potentials"},{"orig":"the more people online, the more potential customers there are","opt":"offers economic potentials"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"can bring foreign funds 把 Q26 与第 4 段 foreign investment 强行拼接；但第 2 段政府重视互联网的原因句里完全没提外资，是张冠李戴。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文只说互联网 may well be the most powerful tool for combating world poverty（很可能是最强大的工具），仍属可能性；选项 can soon wipe out world poverty 加上了 soon 与绝对动词 wipe out，是过度推断。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文确实提到 one to two billion people on the planet will be netted together，但这是技术普及的客观描述，不是政府重视互联网的原因；connects people all over the world 把事实当原因，答非所问。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":27,"stem":"The writer mentioned the case of the United States to justify the policy of____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"providing financial support overseas"},{"key":"B","text":"preventing foreign capital's control"},{"key":"C","text":"building industrial infrastructure"},{"key":"D","text":"accepting foreign investment"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"例证目的题","stemZh":"作者提到美国的例子是为了证明____的政策是正当的。","choicesZh":{"A":"向海外提供财政支持","B":"防止外国资本的控制","C":"建设工业基础设施","D":"接受外国投资"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The writer mentioned the case of the United States to justify the policy of____ 用 to + 动词不定式追问\"举例的目的\"，是典型的例证目的题。","parse":"The writer mentioned the case of the United States to justify the policy of____ 是 \"S + V + O + 不定式状语\" 结构：主句 The writer mentioned the case，to justify ... 作目的状语；选项补的是 policy of 后的名词宾语，明确问\"目的\"。","locateEn":"To take advantage of this tool, some impoverished countries will have to get over their outdated anti-colonial prejudices with respect to foreign investment. ... When the United States built its industrial infrastructure, it didn't have the capital to do so. And that is why America's Second Wave infrastructure—including roads, harbors, highways, ports and so on—was built with foreign investment.","locateZh":"想要用好互联网这件工具，一些贫困国家必须摒弃他们对外资陈旧的反殖民偏见……当年美国修建自己的工业基础设施时，并没有相应资本，这就是为什么美国第二波基础设施——公路、港口、高速、海港等等——都是靠外资建成的。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文中美国是被投资方、英德荷法是出资方；providing financial support overseas 把作者主张写成\"对外提供资金支持\"，与例子里美国\"接受外资\"的角色完全相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文末段以 That doesn't mean ... letting foreign corporations run uncontrolled 作让步性补丁，并非作者举美国例子要支持的主政策；preventing foreign capital's control 把补丁误当成主张，张冠李戴。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"building industrial infrastructure 只是例子里的具体动作（美国当年建第二波基础设施），并不是作者要倡导的政策；考生若只看例子细节，会误把动作当主张。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判结论\"穷国应接受外资\"与 accepting foreign investment 完全对应——例子里的英、德、荷、法投资美国，正是为了佐证这条政策。","pairs":[{"orig":"get over their outdated anti-colonial prejudices with respect to foreign investment","opt":"accepting foreign investment"}]}}}}},{"n":28,"stem":"It seems that now a country's economy depends much on____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"how well-developed it is electronically"},{"key":"B","text":"whether it is prejudiced against immigrants"},{"key":"C","text":"whether it adopts America's industrial pattern"},{"key":"D","text":"how much control it has over foreign corporations"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"推断题","stemZh":"现在一个国家的经济似乎在很大程度上取决于____。","choicesZh":{"A":"它在电子方面的发达程度","B":"它是否对移民抱有偏见","C":"它是否采用美国的工业模式","D":"它对外国公司有多大的控制力"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 It seems that now a country's economy depends much on____ 不直接问原文写了什么，而问\"看起来现在如何\"，需要考生从原文一步合理延伸出来，属推断题。","parse":"It seems that now a country's economy depends much on____ 是 It seems that 引导的从句结构，that 从句中 now 作时间状语，主语 a country's economy，谓语 depends much on，选项补宾语。结构常规，注意 It seems 软化语气，提示推断。","locateEn":"The more foreign capital you have helping you build your Third Wave infrastructure, which today is an electronic infrastructure, the better off you're going to be.","locateZh":"你引来越多的外资帮你建设第三波基础设施——也就是今天的电子基础设施——你的处境就越好。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"电子基础设施越好、国家越富裕，等同于\"经济取决于电子化程度\"，how well-developed it is electronically 是这一推断的最简表达，且没有任何越界。","pairs":[{"orig":"Third Wave infrastructure, which today is an electronic infrastructure","opt":"how well-developed it is electronically"},{"orig":"the better off you're going to be","opt":"how well-developed it is electronically"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文是反对对 foreign investment（外资）的偏见，whether it is prejudiced against immigrants 把对象偷换为 immigrants（移民）——原文只提到 Immigrant Americans built them，与\"偏见\"无关。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文提及 study the history of infrastructure ... in the United States 只是建议穷国研究美国当年的做法，并不是说\"经济现在取决于是否照搬美国模式\"；whether it adopts America's industrial pattern 是过度推断。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"原文末句 That doesn't mean ... letting foreign corporations run uncontrolled 只是补丁，提醒不要放任外资——并不是\"经济取决于对外资公司的控制力\"；how much control it has over foreign corporations 把补丁夸大成核心结论，是以偏概全。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-3","kind":"reading","title":"Text 3","textNo":3,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 3","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-1","text":"Why do so many Americans distrust what they read in their newspapers? The American Society of Newspaper Editors is trying to answer this painful question. The organization is deep into a long self-analysis known as the journalism credibility project."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-2","text":"Sad to say, this project has turned out to be mostly low-level findings about factual errors and spelling and grammar mistakes, combined with lots of head-scratching puzzlement about what in the world those readers really want."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-3","text":"But the sources of distrust go way deeper. Most journalists learn to see the world through a set of standard templates (patterns) into which they plug each day's events. In other words, there is a conventional story line in the newsroom culture that provides a backbone and a ready-made narrative structure for otherwise confusing news."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-4","text":"There exists a social and cultural disconnect between journalists and their readers which helps explain why the \"standard templates\" of the newsroom seem alien to many readers. In a recent survey, questionnaires were sent to reporters in five middle-size cities around the country, plus one large metropolitan area. Then residents in these communities were phoned at random and asked the same questions."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-5","text":"Replies show that compared with other Americans, journalists are more likely to live in upscale neighborhoods, have maids, own Mercedes, and trade stocks, and they're less likely to go to church, do volunteer work, or put down roots in community."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-6","text":"Reporters tend to be part of a broadly defined social and cultural elite, so their work tends to reflect the conventional values of this elite. The astonishing distrust of the news media isn't rooted in inaccuracy or poor reportorial skills but in the daily clash of world views between reporters and their readers."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-3-7","text":"This is an explosive situation for any industry, particularly a declining one. Here is a troubled business that keeps hiring employees whose attitudes vastly annoy the customers. Then it sponsors lots of symposiums and a credibility project dedicated to wondering why customers are annoyed and fleeing in large numbers. But it never seems to get around to noticing the cultural and class biases that so many former buyers are complaining about. If it did, it would open up its diversity program, now focused narrowly on race and gender, and look for reporters who differ broadly by outlook, values, education, and class."}]},"questions":[{"n":29,"stem":"What is the passage mainly about?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"needs of the readers all over the world."},{"key":"B","text":"causes of the public disappointment about newspapers."},{"key":"C","text":"origins of the declining newspaper industry."},{"key":"D","text":"aims of a journalism credibility project."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"这篇文章主要讲述了什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"全世界读者的需求。","B":"公众对报纸失望的原因。","C":"报纸行业衰落的起源。","D":"新闻可信度项目的目标。"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 What is the passage mainly about? 直接问 passage 整体讲了什么，没有任何局部信息词。","parse":"What is the passage mainly about? 是一个标准的 wh 疑问句，主干 the passage is about what，无从句、无否定、无比较，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"needs of the readers all over the world. 把读者范围扩大到 all over the world，但全文限定在 so many Americans，且讨论的不是 needs 而是 disappointment 的成因。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"首段问句确立议题、第六、七段给出根因，主线全部围绕「公众失望的原因」，B 是唯一同时覆盖议题与原因的选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"Why do so many Americans distrust what they read in their newspapers?","opt":"causes of the public disappointment about newspapers."},{"orig":"The astonishing distrust of the news media isn't rooted in inaccuracy or poor reportorial skills but in the daily clash of world views between reporters and their readers.","opt":"causes of the public disappointment about newspapers."},{"orig":"But it never seems to get around to noticing the cultural and class biases that so many former buyers are complaining about.","opt":"causes of the public disappointment about newspapers."}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"origins of the declining newspaper industry. 把全文聚焦点偷换成「报业衰落的起源」。原文虽在 particularly a declining one 顺带提到衰落，但全篇主线是公众不信任的成因，不是衰落史。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"aims of a journalism credibility project. 把 credibility project 当全文主角，但该项目在文中只是「被批评的研究对象」，作者借 P2 否定其成效后转入更深原因，全文从不讨论其 aims。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":30,"stem":"The results of the journalism credibility project turned out to be____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"quite trustworthy"},{"key":"B","text":"somewhat contradictory"},{"key":"C","text":"very illuminating"},{"key":"D","text":"rather superficial"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"新闻可信度项目的结果最终证明是____。","choicesZh":{"A":"相当可信","B":"有些矛盾","C":"很有启发性","D":"相当肤浅"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The results of the journalism credibility project turned out to be____. 是个待补全的陈述句，要的是原文中关于结果的客观转述。","parse":"The results of the journalism credibility project turned out to be____. 主干为 the results turned out to be ___，turn out to be 意为「结果是/原来是」，空格填表语形容词；结构清晰，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Sad to say, this project has turned out to be mostly low-level findings about factual errors and spelling and grammar mistakes, combined with lots of head-scratching puzzlement about what in the world those readers really want.","locateZh":"遗憾的是，该项目最终得出的不过是关于事实错误和拼写、语法错误的低层次发现，再加上对读者究竟想要什么的一脸茫然。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"quite trustworthy 评价的是结果「是否可信」，但原文从未质疑结果真假，只批评其层次低；选项把「层次」换成了「可信度」。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"somewhat contradictory 要求原文给出「前后/内部相互矛盾」的证据，但定位句只说结果浅、不说结果之间打架。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"very illuminating 的极性是褒义、表示「很有启发」，与 Sad to say 起头的负面评价以及 low-level / head-scratching puzzlement 的轻蔑色彩完全相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"定位句把项目成果同时贴上「低层次」和「对核心问题没头绪」两个标签，二者并集恰是「流于表面」的同义表达，rather superficial 是唯一对得上的形容词。","pairs":[{"orig":"low-level findings about factual errors and spelling and grammar mistakes","opt":"rather superficial"},{"orig":"lots of head-scratching puzzlement about what in the world those readers really want","opt":"rather superficial"}]}}}}},{"n":31,"stem":"The basic problem of journalists as pointed out by the writer lies in their____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"working attitude"},{"key":"B","text":"conventional lifestyle"},{"key":"C","text":"world outlook"},{"key":"D","text":"educational background"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者指出的新闻工作者的根本问题在于他们的____。","choicesZh":{"A":"工作态度","B":"传统的生活方式","C":"世界观","D":"教育背景"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 The basic problem of journalists as pointed out by the writer lies in their____. 直接问作者点出的根本问题落在哪一维度，是对原文判断句的客观提取。","parse":"The basic problem of journalists as pointed out by the writer lies in their____. 主干 the basic problem lies in their ___，as pointed out by the writer 为过去分词短语作后置定语修饰 problem，限定信息来源是「作者所指」；their 指代 journalists，空格填名词。","locateEn":"The astonishing distrust of the news media isn't rooted in inaccuracy or poor reportorial skills but in the daily clash of world views between reporters and their readers.","locateZh":"对新闻媒体那种令人吃惊的不信任，根源不在于报道不准确或记者技能差，而在于记者与读者之间每天发生的世界观冲撞。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"working attitude（工作态度）属于 inaccuracy or poor reportorial skills 所涵盖的「工作层面」原因，被作者明确归入 not A 一侧。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"conventional lifestyle 对应的是 P5 的生活方式数据（住高档社区、有女佣、开奔驰），那只是 world views 的具象表征，不是作者点的「根本问题」。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"在 not rooted in 报道技能 but in 世界观 的明确对照里，作者一笔否掉「工作技能」型解释，把根本问题点在世界观上，world outlook 是该 B 项的近义浓缩。","pairs":[{"orig":"the daily clash of world views between reporters and their readers","opt":"world outlook"},{"orig":"Reporters tend to be part of a broadly defined social and cultural elite, so their work tends to reflect the conventional values of this elite.","opt":"world outlook"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"educational background 直到 reporters who differ broadly by outlook, values, education, and class 才作为多样性维度之一被提及，原文从未将「教育背景」单独点为 basic problem。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":32,"stem":"Despite its efforts, the newspaper industry still cannot satisfy the readers owing to its____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"failure to realize its real problem"},{"key":"B","text":"tendency to hire annoying reporters"},{"key":"C","text":"likeliness to do inaccurate reporting"},{"key":"D","text":"prejudice in matters of race and gender"}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"尽管做出了努力,报纸行业仍然无法满足读者,原因在于其____。","choicesZh":{"A":"未能认识到其真正的问题","B":"倾向于雇用令人讨厌的记者","C":"可能进行不准确的报道","D":"在种族和性别问题上的偏见"},"analysis":{"type":"题干 Despite its efforts, the newspaper industry still cannot satisfy the readers owing to its____. 是一个完整因果陈述待补全，问的就是原文给出的具体原因。","parse":"Despite its efforts, the newspaper industry still cannot satisfy the readers owing to its____. 句首 Despite its efforts 为让步状语；主干 the newspaper industry cannot satisfy the readers；owing to its____ 为原因状语补充原因，its 指代 the newspaper industry，空格填名词性短语。","locateEn":"But it never seems to get around to noticing the cultural and class biases that so many former buyers are complaining about.","locateZh":"但它似乎从来没真正去关注那些被大量老读者抱怨的文化和阶级偏见。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文「始终没注意到」被作者明确判为「行业屡战屡败的根因」，选项以「未能意识到其真正的问题」作动名词化浓缩，语义与归因方向完全一致。","pairs":[{"orig":"it never seems to get around to noticing the cultural and class biases that so many former buyers are complaining about","opt":"failure to realize its real problem"},{"orig":"The astonishing distrust of the news media isn't rooted in inaccuracy or poor reportorial skills but in the daily clash of world views","opt":"failure to realize its real problem"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"tendency to hire annoying reporters 描述的是 keeps hiring employees whose attitudes vastly annoy the customers 这一现象本身，作者用它作为问题的表征，而非作者归纳的根本原因。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"likeliness to do inaccurate reporting 直接对应 inaccuracy or poor reportorial skills，而那是作者明确用 not A but B 排除掉的旧因。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"prejudice in matters of race and gender 把 its diversity program, now focused narrowly on race and gender 反向曲解——原文意思是 diversity 项目只盯着 race/gender 而忽略 outlook/values/class，并不是说报业本身存在种族性别偏见。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-4","kind":"reading","title":"Text 4","textNo":4,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 4","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-1","text":"The world is going through the biggest wave of mergers and acquisitions ever witnessed. The process sweeps from hyperactive America to Europe and reaches the emerging countries with unsurpassed might. Many in these countries are looking at this process and worrying: \"Won't the wave of business concentration turn into an uncontrollable anti-competitive force?\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-2","text":"There's no question that the big are getting bigger and more powerful. Multinational corporations accounted for less than 20% of international trade in 1982. Today the figure is more than 25% and growing rapidly. International affiliates account for a fast-growing segment of production in economies that open up and welcome foreign investment. In Argentina, for instance, after the reforms of the early 1990s, multinationals went from 43% to almost 70% of the industrial production of the 200 largest firms. This phenomenon has created serious concerns over the role of smaller economic firms, of national businessmen and over the ultimate stability of the world economy."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-3","text":"I believe that the most important forces behind the massive M&A wave are the same that underlie the globalization process: falling transportation and communication costs, lower trade and investment barriers and enlarged markets that require enlarged operations capable of meeting customers' demands. All these are beneficial, not detrimental, to consumers. As productivity grows, the world's wealth increases."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-4","text":"Examples of benefits or costs of the current concentration wave are scanty. Yet it is hard to imagine that the merger of a few oil firms today could re-create the same threats to competition that were feared nearly a century ago in the U.S., when the Standard Oil trust was broken up. The mergers of telecom companies, such as WorldCom, hardly seem to bring higher prices for consumers or a reduction in the pace of technical progress. On the contrary, the price of communications is coming down fast. In cars, too, concentration is increasing—witness Daimler and Chrysler, Renault and Nissan-but it does not appear that consumers are being hurt."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-4-5","text":"Yet the fact remains that the merger movement must be watched. A few weeks ago, Alan Greenspan warned against the megamergers in the banking industry. Who is going to supervise, regulate and operate as lender of last resort with the gigantic banks that are being created? Won't multinationals shift production from one place to another when a nation gets too strict about infringements to fair competition? And should one country take upon itself the role of \"defending competition\" on issues that affect many other nations, as in the U.S. vs. Microsoft case?"}]},"questions":[{"n":33,"stem":"What is the typical trend of businesses today?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"to take in more foreign funds."},{"key":"B","text":"to invest more abroad."},{"key":"C","text":"to combine and become bigger."},{"key":"D","text":"to trade with more countries."}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"主旨题","stemZh":"当今企业的典型趋势是什么?","choicesZh":{"A":"吸收更多外国资金。","B":"在海外进行更多投资。","C":"合并并变得更大。","D":"与更多国家进行贸易。"},"analysis":{"type":"What is the typical trend of businesses today? 问的是\"当下企业的典型走向\"，覆盖全文话题而非某段细节，故判为主旨题。","parse":"What is the typical trend of businesses today? 是单层 wh-疑问句，主干 What is the typical trend，of businesses today 整体修饰 trend，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"to take in more foreign funds. 把\"引进外资\"作为典型趋势；原文 economies that open up and welcome foreign investment 只在解释跨国公司占比上升的背景时一带而过，作者所讲的\"典型趋势\"是企业合并而非吸纳外资，是以偏概全。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"to invest more abroad. 抓住\"对外投资\"这一侧面；原文虽提及 multinationals 在他国生产，但全文主线是\"企业相互兼并、变大\"而非\"企业更多对外投资\"，仍是以偏概全。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"to combine and become bigger. 同时涵盖首段 mergers and acquisitions 和第二段 getting bigger and more powerful，是全文主线的最简表述。","pairs":[{"orig":"The world is going through the biggest wave of mergers and acquisitions ever witnessed.","opt":"to combine and become bigger."},{"orig":"the big are getting bigger and more powerful","opt":"to combine and become bigger."}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"to trade with more countries. 着眼于\"贸易伙伴增多\"；原文 P2 谈及 international trade 只是数据背景，文章主线是合并集中化，不是\"扩大贸易伙伴\"，仍属以偏概全。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":34,"stem":"According to the author, one of the driving forces behind M&A wave is____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the greater customer demands."},{"key":"B","text":"a surplus supply for the market."},{"key":"C","text":"a growing productivity."},{"key":"D","text":"the increase of the world's wealth."}],"answer":"A","explanation":{"answer":"A","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据作者的观点,并购浪潮背后的驱动力之一是____","choicesZh":{"A":"更大的客户需求。","B":"市场供应过剩。","C":"生产力的增长。","D":"世界财富的增加。"},"analysis":{"type":"one of the driving forces 指向原文一处具体列举，找到列举句逐项核对即可，属典型细节题。","parse":"According to the author, one of the driving forces behind M&A wave is____ 是\"主+系+表\"结构的不完整句，According to the author 为状语，one of the driving forces 为主语，behind M&A wave 修饰 forces，空格处补表语；结构清晰无陷阱。","locateEn":"I believe that the most important forces behind the massive M&A wave are the same that underlie the globalization process: falling transportation and communication costs, lower trade and investment barriers and enlarged markets that require enlarged operations capable of meeting customers' demands.","locateZh":"我认为推动这一巨大并购浪潮的最重要力量，与推动全球化进程的力量相同：运输和通信成本的下降、贸易和投资壁垒的降低，以及为满足顾客需求而需要扩大经营的扩展型市场。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"在四个选项中，只有 the greater customer demands 与定位句列举的第三项 meeting customers' demands 等值，其余项与列举内容均无直接映射。","pairs":[{"orig":"enlarged markets that require enlarged operations capable of meeting customers' demands","opt":"the greater customer demands"}]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"a surplus supply for the market 讲的是\"市场供给过剩\"，原文 P3 中三项驱动力（成本下降、壁垒降低、市场扩大）均不涉及\"供给过剩\"，是无中生有。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"原文 As productivity grows, the world's wealth increases. 把生产率增长写成并购带来的\"结果\"而非\"驱动力\"；a growing productivity 把结果当成原因，属与原文相反/因果倒置。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"the increase of the world's wealth 与 the world's wealth increases 一致，但原文中它同样是\"生产力增长\"之后的结果链条尾端，并非推动并购的\"driving force\"，属答非所问/与原文相反。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":35,"stem":"From paragraph 4 we can infer that____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the increasing concentration is certain to hurt consumers"},{"key":"B","text":"WorldCom serves as a good example of both benefits and costs"},{"key":"C","text":"the costs of the globalization process are enormous"},{"key":"D","text":"the Standard Oil trust might have threatened competition"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"推断题","stemZh":"从第4段我们可以推断出____。","choicesZh":{"A":"日益加剧的集中化肯定会损害消费者","B":"WorldCom是收益和成本兼具的一个好例子","C":"全球化进程的成本是巨大的","D":"标准石油托拉斯可能曾威胁过竞争"},"analysis":{"type":"we can infer that 中的 infer 是推断题的标志词，要求基于原文做一步合理推理。","parse":"From paragraph 4 we can infer that____. 主干 we can infer that...，From paragraph 4 是地点状语限定推断的依据范围；空格处补 that 引导的宾语从句，结构平铺直叙，无陷阱。","locateEn":"Yet it is hard to imagine that the merger of a few oil firms today could re-create the same threats to competition that were feared nearly a century ago in the U.S., when the Standard Oil trust was broken up.","locateZh":"然而很难想象，今日少数石油公司的合并能够再现近一个世纪前在美国所担忧的、那种对竞争的威胁——当年正是基于这种担忧拆解了 Standard Oil 托拉斯。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"原文 P4 反复用 hardly seem to bring higher prices、it does not appear that consumers are being hurt 等表述否认\"集中化必然伤害消费者\"；the increasing concentration is certain to hurt consumers 用 is certain to 反着说，是与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"原文用 WorldCom 仅作\"未推高价格\"的正面例证，未提及任何 costs；WorldCom serves as a good example of both benefits and costs 凭空给 WorldCom 加上\"costs\"一侧，是无中生有/过度推断。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"第 4 段讨论的是\"并购集中化\"的代价，不是全球化的代价；the costs of the globalization process are enormous 把话题切换到 globalization 且用 enormous 夸大程度，属于张冠李戴 + 过度推断。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"在四个选项中，the Standard Oil trust might have threatened competition 是唯一一个仅做一步推理、且严格落在定位句让步前提上的选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"the same threats to competition that were feared nearly a century ago in the U.S., when the Standard Oil trust was broken up","opt":"the Standard Oil trust might have threatened competition"}]}}}}},{"n":36,"stem":"Toward the new business wave, the writer's attitude can be said to be____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"optimistic"},{"key":"B","text":"objective"},{"key":"C","text":"pessimistic"},{"key":"D","text":"biased"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"态度题","stemZh":"对于新的商业浪潮,作者的态度可以说是____。","choicesZh":{"A":"乐观的","B":"客观的","C":"悲观的","D":"有偏见的"},"analysis":{"type":"the writer's attitude 直接问作者态度，是态度题最标准的题干形式。","parse":"Toward the new business wave, the writer's attitude can be said to be____. 主干 the writer's attitude can be said to be...，Toward the new business wave 为方向状语限定态度的指向对象；can be said to be 是较弱的判断表达，提示答案可能是较温和而非极端的态度词。","locateEn":"","locateZh":"","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"optimistic 仅吻合第 3、4 段的正面评价，却覆盖不了第 5 段以 Yet the fact remains that the merger movement must be watched. 开头的多重监管疑虑，属以偏概全。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"作者同时陈述并购的好处和潜在风险，且语气克制无情绪化用词，objective 是四项中唯一能同时容纳正反两面的态度词。","pairs":[{"orig":"All these are beneficial, not detrimental, to consumers.","opt":"objective"},{"orig":"Yet the fact remains that the merger movement must be watched.","opt":"objective"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"pessimistic 假设作者主调\"悲观\"，但作者在第 3、4 段明确肯定并购的好处 it does not appear that consumers are being hurt，是与原文相反。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"biased 暗示作者立场\"有偏见\"；但作者使用 hardly seem、it does not appear、must be watched 等克制措辞，并主动提出反方疑虑，没有偏颇标志，是无中生有。","pairs":[]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-a-5","kind":"reading","title":"Text 5","textNo":5,"directions":"","points":10,"passage":{"title":"Text 5","paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-1","text":"When I decided to quit my full time employment it never occurred to me that I might become a part of a new international trend. A lateral move that hurt my pride and blocked my professional progress prompted me to abandon my relatively high profile career although, in the manner of a disgraced government minister, I covered my exit by claiming \"I wanted to spend more time with my family\"."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-2","text":"Curiously, some two-and-a-half years and two novels later, my experiment in what the Americans term \"downshifting\" has turned my tired excuse into an absolute reality. I have been transformed from a passionate advocate of the philosophy of \"having it all\", preached by Linda Kelsey for the past seven years in the pages of She magazine, into a woman who is happy to settle for a bit of everything."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-3","text":"I have discovered, as perhaps Kelsey will after her much-publicized resignation from the editorship of She after a build-up of stress, that abandoning the doctrine of \"juggling your life\", and making the alternative move into \"downshifting\" brings with it far greater rewards than financial success and social status. Nothing could persuade me to return to the kind of life Kelsey used to advocate and I once enjoyed: 12-hour working days, pressured deadlines, the fearful strain of office politics and the limitations of being a parent on \"quality time\"."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-4","text":"In America, the move away from juggling to a simpler, less materialistic lifestyle is a well-established trend. Downshifting—also known in America as \"voluntary simplicity\" has, ironically, even bred a new area of what might be termed anticonsumerism. There are a number of bestselling downshifting self-help books for people who want to simplify their lives; there are newsletters, such as The Tightwad Gazette, that give hundreds of thousands of Americans useful tips on anything from recycling their cling-film to making their own soap; there are even support groups for those who want to achieve the mid-'90s equivalent of dropping out."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-5","text":"While in America the trend started as a reaction to the economic decline—after the mass redundancies caused by downsizing in the late '80s—and is still linked to the politics of thrift, in Britain, at least among the middle-class downshifters of my acquaintance, we have different reasons for seeking to simplify our lives."},{"id":"p-section2-part-a-5-6","text":"For the women of my generation who were urged to keep juggling through the '80s, downshifting in the mid-'90s is not so much a search for the mythical good life—growing your own organic vegetables, and risking turning into one—as a personal recognition of your limitations."}]},"questions":[{"n":37,"stem":"Which of the following is true according to paragraph 1?","options":[{"key":"A","text":"Full-time employment is a new international trend."},{"key":"B","text":"The writer was compelled by circumstances to leave her job."},{"key":"C","text":"\"A lateral move\" means stepping out of full-time employment."},{"key":"D","text":"The writer was only too eager to spend more time with her family."}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据第一段,以下哪项是正确的?","choicesZh":{"A":"全职工作是一种新的国际趋势。","B":"作者被环境所迫离开了她的工作。","C":"\"横向调动\"意味着退出全职工作。","D":"作者非常渴望花更多时间陪伴家人。"},"analysis":{"type":"Which of the following is true according to paragraph 1 直接要求在四个陈述里挑出与原文一致的事实，没有 infer/imply/mainly 等字眼。","parse":"Which of the following is true according to paragraph 1 是一个典型的 which 引导的疑问句，主句省略，which 充当主语，of the following 限定范围，according to paragraph 1 是状语，结构清晰、无陷阱。","locateEn":"A lateral move that hurt my pride and blocked my professional progress prompted me to abandon my relatively high profile career although, in the manner of a disgraced government minister, I covered my exit by claiming \"I wanted to spend more time with my family\".","locateZh":"一次平调伤了我的自尊、又堵死了我的职业晋升，迫使我放弃了相对高调的职业生涯；不过我像一位失势的政府部长那样，用一句\"我想多花点时间陪家人\"为自己的离场遮羞。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"Full-time employment is a new international trend 把 a new international trend 的主语偷换成 full-time employment；原文说的是\"辞掉全职\"成了新趋势，正好相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判说被外部环境逼走，B 用 compelled by circumstances 准确对应 prompted by a lateral move，且与 covered my exit 暗示的非自愿离场吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"A lateral move that hurt my pride and blocked my professional progress prompted me to abandon my relatively high profile career","opt":"The writer was compelled by circumstances to leave her job"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"\"A lateral move\" means stepping out of full-time employment 把 A lateral move（公司内部平级调动）解释成\"辞掉全职\"；原文中 lateral move 是 prompted 的主语，是辞职的诱因，而非辞职本身。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"The writer was only too eager to spend more time with her family 把作者明确指出的托词 I wanted to spend more time with my family 当成真实意愿；原文 covered my exit by claiming 已亮明这是遮羞之辞。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":38,"stem":"The writer's experiment shows that downshifting____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"enables her to realize her dream"},{"key":"B","text":"helps her mold a new philosophy of life"},{"key":"C","text":"prompts her to abandon her high social status"},{"key":"D","text":"leads her to accept the doctrine of She magazine"}],"answer":"B","explanation":{"answer":"B","type":"细节题","stemZh":"作者的实验表明降速生活____","choicesZh":{"A":"使她实现了自己的梦想","B":"帮助她塑造了新的人生哲学","C":"促使她放弃了高社会地位","D":"引导她接受She杂志的理念"},"analysis":{"type":"The writer's experiment shows that downshifting____ 要求选出原文已经表述出来的 shows 的内容，没有要求做超出文本的推理。","parse":"The writer's experiment shows that downshifting____ 是一个被省略宾语从句的陈述句，四个选项分别充当 that 从句的谓语部分；只需把选项嵌入主语 downshifting 后判读即可。","locateEn":"I have been transformed from a passionate advocate of the philosophy of \"having it all\", preached by Linda Kelsey for the past seven years in the pages of She magazine, into a woman who is happy to settle for a bit of everything.","locateZh":"我已经从 Linda Kelsey 过去七年在 She 杂志里反复鼓吹的\"一切都要拥有\"这一哲学的热情信徒，转变为一个乐于在每件事上都只求一点的女人。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"enables her to realize her dream 中的 dream 在原文里没有任何对应；作者描述的是 settle for a bit of everything，即降低期望、退守安稳，与\"实现梦想\"相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"预判说\"对人生信条的重塑\"，B 项 mold a new philosophy of life 一字不差地表达了\"塑造新人生哲学\"，与 transformed from...into... 高度吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"I have been transformed from a passionate advocate of the philosophy of \"having it all\"...into a woman who is happy to settle for a bit of everything","opt":"helps her mold a new philosophy of life"}]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"prompts her to abandon her high social status 描述的是\"促使她放弃高地位\"——这属于 P1 中辞职的动机，不是 P2 中实验显示出的结果，与 experiment shows that 的设问对象错位。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"leads her to accept the doctrine of She magazine 把 She 杂志的信条当作她接受的对象；原文 passionate advocate of the philosophy of \"having it all\", preached by Linda Kelsey...in the pages of She magazine 与 abandoning the doctrine of \"juggling your life\" 显示作者是从该信条转出而非走入。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":39,"stem":"\"Juggling one's life\" probably means living a life characterized by____.","options":[{"key":"A","text":"non-materialistic lifestyle"},{"key":"B","text":"a bit of everything"},{"key":"C","text":"extreme stress"},{"key":"D","text":"anti-consumerism"}],"answer":"C","explanation":{"answer":"C","type":"词义句意题","stemZh":"\"兼顾多重生活\"可能意味着过一种以____为特点的生活。","choicesZh":{"A":"非物质主义的生活方式","B":"什么都涉及一点","C":"极度压力","D":"反消费主义"},"analysis":{"type":"probably means living a life characterized by 明显是要求解释引号短语的含义，属于典型词义句意题。","parse":"\"Juggling one's life\" probably means living a life characterized by____ 主语为带引号短语，谓语 means 后接动名词短语 living a life，再用过去分词 characterized by 引出后置定语，空格处即为该定语的核心名词。","locateEn":"Nothing could persuade me to return to the kind of life Kelsey used to advocate and I once enjoyed: 12-hour working days, pressured deadlines, the fearful strain of office politics and the limitations of being a parent on \"quality time\".","locateZh":"没有什么能说服我回到 Kelsey 过去所鼓吹、我也曾享受的那种生活：每天 12 小时工作、deadline 压迫、办公室政治的可怕煎熬，以及只能在\"亲子高质量时间\"里做家长的种种局限。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"non-materialistic lifestyle 描述的恰是作者所选择的 voluntary simplicity 一类的极简生活，而 juggling your life 是她抛弃的旧生活，二者方向相反。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"a bit of everything 出自 settle for a bit of everything，描述的是作者转变后的新生活方式，而非 juggling 那种\"既要又要\"。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"预判说\"极端高压\"，C 项 extreme stress 直接对应；与 the fearful strain 在情绪强度上也吻合。","pairs":[{"orig":"12-hour working days, pressured deadlines, the fearful strain of office politics and the limitations of being a parent on \"quality time\"","opt":"extreme stress"}]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"anti-consumerism 出自 anticonsumerism，是 downshifting 衍生的反向运动，与高压 juggling 的物欲并举完全对立。","pairs":[]}}}}},{"n":40,"stem":"According to the passage, downshifting emerged in the U.S. as a result of____","options":[{"key":"A","text":"the quick pace of modern life"},{"key":"B","text":"man's adventurous spirit"},{"key":"C","text":"man's search for mythical experiences"},{"key":"D","text":"the economic situation"}],"answer":"D","explanation":{"answer":"D","type":"细节题","stemZh":"根据文章,降速生活在美国出现是____的结果","choicesZh":{"A":"现代生活的快节奏","B":"人类的冒险精神","C":"人类对神秘体验的追寻","D":"经济形势"},"analysis":{"type":"downshifting emerged in the U.S. as a result of____ 询问的是一个客观因果关系，且范围限定在美国，回文可直接核对，无需推理。","parse":"According to the passage, downshifting emerged in the U.S. as a result of____ 主句结构为 downshifting emerged，状语 in the U.S. 和 as a result of___ 分别给出地点和原因，空格充当 of 的宾语。","locateEn":"While in America the trend started as a reaction to the economic decline—after the mass redundancies caused by downsizing in the late '80s—and is still linked to the politics of thrift, in Britain, at least among the middle-class downshifters of my acquaintance, we have different reasons for seeking to simplify our lives.","locateZh":"在美国，这股潮流的兴起是对经济衰退的反应——出现在 80 年代末大裁员之后——而且至今仍与节俭政治相连；而在英国，至少在我认识的中产阶级 downshifters 中，我们追求简化生活则另有原因。","options":{"A":{"flag":"","note":"the quick pace of modern life 中的 quick pace 在原文里没有任何对应；原文给出的是经济衰退，而非现代生活节奏。","pairs":[]},"B":{"flag":"","note":"man's adventurous spirit 中的\"冒险精神\"在文中没有任何痕迹；作者对 downshifting 的原因解释是经济与节俭政治，与冒险精神无关。","pairs":[]},"C":{"flag":"","note":"man's search for mythical experiences 把 the mythical good life 偷换成 mythical experiences；原文用 the mythical good life 是说英国女性 downshifting 时并非追求这种田园神话（not so much...as...），且只描述英国、与美国 downshifting 起因无关。","pairs":[]},"D":{"flag":"","note":"预判说\"经济衰退所致\"，D 项 the economic situation 把 economic decline 一般化为\"经济状况\"；再结合 the mass redundancies caused by downsizing in the late '80s 这一裁员事实，D 是唯一与经济相关的选项。","pairs":[{"orig":"the trend started as a reaction to the economic decline","opt":"the economic situation"}]}}}}}]},{"id":"section2-part-b","kind":"translation","title":"Section II Part C 英译汉","directions":"Directions: Read the following text carefully and then translate the underlined segments into Chinese. Write your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. ( 10 points)","points":10,"passage":{"paragraphs":[{"id":"p-section2-part-b-1","text":"In less than 30 years' time the Star Trek holodeck will be a reality. Direct links between the brain's nervous system and a computer will also create full sensory virtual environments, allowing virtual vacations like those in the film Total Recall."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-2","text":"(41) There will be television chat shows hosted by robots, and cars with pollution monitors that will disable them when they offend. (42) Children will play with dolls equipped with personality chips, computers with in-built personalities will be regarded as workmates rather than tools, relaxation will be in front of smell television, and the digital age will have arrived."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-3","text":"According to BT's futurologist, Ian Pearson, these are among the developments scheduled for the first few decades of the new millennium(a period of 1,000 years), when supercomputers will dramatically accelerate progress in all areas of life."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-4","text":"(43) Pearson has pieced together the work of hundreds of researchers around the world to produce a unique millennium technology calendar that gives the latest dates when we can expect hundreds of key breakthroughs and discoveries to take place. Some of the biggest developments will be in medicine, including an extended life expectancy and dozens of artificial organs coming into use between now and 2040."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-5","text":"Pearson also predicts a breakthrough in computer-human links. \"By linking directly to our nervous system, computers could pick up what we feel and, hopefully, simulate feeling too so that we can start to develop full sensory environments, rather like the holidays in Total Recall or the Star Trek holodeck,\" he says. (44) But that, Pearson points out, is only the start of man-machine integration: \"It will be the beginning of the long process of integration that will ultimately lead to a fully electronic human before the end of the next century.\""},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-6","text":"Through his research, Pearson is able to put dates to most of the breakthroughs that can be predicted. However, there are still no forecasts for when faster-than-light travel will be available, or when human cloning will be perfected, or when time travel will be possible. But he does expect social problems as a result of technological advances. A boom in neighborhood surveillance cameras will, for example, cause problems in 2010, while the arrival of synthetic lifelike robots will mean people may not be able to distinguish between their human friends and the droids."},{"id":"p-section2-part-b-7","text":"(45) And home appliances will also become so smart that controlling and operating them will result in the breakout of a new psychological disorder—kitchen rage."}]},"sentences":[{"n":41,"en":"There will be television chat shows hosted by robots, and cars with pollution monitors that will disable them when they offend.","refZh":"届时将会出现由机器人主持的电视访谈节目，以及装有污染监测装置的汽车——一旦这些汽车违规排放，监测装置就会让它们无法行驶。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"There will be television chat shows","lit":"将会出现电视访谈节目","role":"（主干 There be 结构（并列第一项））","note":"难点： chat show 译“访谈/脱口秀节目” chat show 不是“聊天表演”，而是英式英语里固定指 television chat shows 这类“电视访谈节目/脱口秀”。考研里这类英美文化词不直译字面，要还原成中文里对应的节目类型名。"},{"en":"hosted by robots,","lit":"由机器人主持的","role":"（过去分词短语作 chat shows 的后置定语）","note":"难点： 后置定语前移译“…的” hosted by robots 是修饰 chat shows 的过去分词短语，汉译时不能保留英文“节目—被机器人主持”的语序，要前移成“由机器人主持的电视访谈节目”，这是后置定语汉化的通法。"},{"en":"and cars with pollution monitors","lit":"以及装有污染监测器的汽车","role":"（主干并列第二项（与 chat shows 并列）+ with 介词短语作定语）","note":"难点： with 短语作后置定语、pollution monitor 具体化 with pollution monitors 不是状语，而是修饰 cars 的“带有…”定语，汉化时同样前移为“装有/配有污染监测装置的汽车”。pollution monitor 是合成名词，要具体化为“污染（排放）监测装置”，不要笼统译“污染器”。"},{"en":"that will disable them when they offend.","lit":"当它们违规排污时使它们无法运行","role":"（that 引导的定语从句修饰 pollution monitors；内嵌 when 时间状语从句）","note":"难点： them 与 they 都回指 cars，offend 取“违规排污”义 这里有两个考生易翻车的点：① them 与 they 都不指 monitors，而回指 cars——能“排放污染”的是汽车，能被“禁用”的也是汽车；② offend 是熟词僻义，本义“冒犯”，此处在污染语境下取“违规/违章（排放）”，可参 cars with pollution monitors that will disable them when they offend 整句逻辑确认。disable 译“使无法行驶/禁用”，不要硬译“使残疾”。"}]},{"n":42,"en":"Children will play with dolls equipped with personality chips, computers with in-built personalities will be regarded as workmates rather than tools, relaxation will be in front of smell television, and the digital age will have arrived.","refZh":"孩子们将与装有个性芯片的玩偶一起玩耍，内置个性的电脑将被视为同事而非工具，人们将在气味电视机前休闲放松，到那时数字时代就已经到来了。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Children will play with dolls equipped with personality chips,","lit":"孩子们将玩装有个性芯片的玩偶","role":"（并列分句一（主干：Children will play with dolls + 过去分词后置定语））","note":"难点： equipped with 是后置定语，不是谓语 equipped with personality chips 是过去分词短语修饰 dolls，不是说 dolls 主动“装备”了什么。要前移译成“装有个性芯片的玩偶”。personality chip 字面“个性芯片”即可，但要意识到这是科幻语境下的造词。"},{"en":"computers with in-built personalities will be regarded as workmates rather than tools,","lit":"内置个性的电脑将被视为工友而非工具","role":"（并列分句二（主干：computers will be regarded as））","note":"难点： 被动转主动 + rather than 译“而非” will be regarded as 是被动语态，汉译可转主动“人们会把…视为…”，或用无主句“…会被视为…”；rather than 是对比连词，固定译“而不是/而非”，不要漏掉这层对比关系。in-built 与第一分句的 equipped with 呼应，都是“内置”的意思，可统一术语。workmate 译“同事/工友”，比“工作伙伴”更接地气。"},{"en":"relaxation will be in front of smell television,","lit":"休闲将在气味电视机前进行","role":"（并列分句三（主干：relaxation will be + 地点状语））","note":"难点： 抽象名词 relaxation 具体化为动作 relaxation 是抽象名词，直译“放松”作主语在汉语里别扭，要具体化为动作“人们休闲/放松时”作状语，让谓语“在…前”有落脚点。smell television 是“气味电视”这一造词，保留字面即可。这是抽象名词具体化的典型操作。"},{"en":"and the digital age will have arrived.","lit":"数字时代就已经到来了","role":"（并列分句四（主干：digital age will have arrived，将来完成时））","note":"难点： 将来完成时译“到那时…就已经…” will have arrived 是将来完成时，强调“到那个未来时间点为止已经完成”，汉译要补上“到那时/届时…就已经…”的时间锚，呼应前三句描绘的种种未来景象。这是该时态的固定汉化套路。"}]},{"n":43,"en":"Pearson has pieced together the work of hundreds of researchers around the world to produce a unique millennium technology calendar that gives the latest dates when we can expect hundreds of key breakthroughs and discoveries to take place.","refZh":"Pearson 汇集了全世界数百名研究人员的研究成果，从而推出了一份独特的千年技术大事年表——上面列出了我们预期数百项重大突破和发现得以实现的最迟日期。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"Pearson has pieced together the work of hundreds of researchers around the world","lit":"Pearson 汇集了全世界数百名研究者的工作成果","role":"（主干（主谓宾）+ of 短语作定语）","note":"难点： piece together 译“汇集/整理”，work 译“研究成果” piece together 是固定短语，本义“把碎片拼起来”，引申为“汇集、整理、综合”，对应学术语境下的“整合研究成果”。work 在科研语境下不是“工作”，是“研究/成果”，是熟词僻义。around the world 译“全世界/世界各地”，作 researchers 的后置定语。"},{"en":"to produce a unique millennium technology calendar","lit":"以制作出一份独特的千年技术日历","role":"（不定式短语作目的状语）","note":"难点： to do 译目的“以/从而/旨在” 不定式 to produce 表目的，汉译用“以/从而/旨在”等连接词承上。millennium 是“千年/千禧年”，technology calendar 字面“技术日历”，这里指列出各项技术突破时间表的清单，可意译为“千年技术大事年表”，更贴汉语。"},{"en":"that gives the latest dates","lit":"上面列出了最迟日期","role":"（that 引导的定语从句，修饰 calendar）","note":"难点： latest 取“最迟/最晚”而非“最新” latest 有两义：① 最新的；② 最迟/最晚的。这里搭配 dates when we can expect…to take place（预期…发生的日期），逻辑上应是“我们预期某事发生的最晚截止日期”——即最迟也要到这个日子，常被考生误译成“最新日期”。这是典型熟词僻义陷阱。"},{"en":"when we can expect hundreds of key breakthroughs and discoveries to take place.","lit":"我们可以预期数百项关键突破与发现将在这些日期发生","role":"（when 引导的定语从句，修饰 dates）","note":"难点： when 引导定语从句而非时间状语，expect…to do 译“预期…发生” when 在这里不是“当…时”这种状语连词，而是关系副词，修饰 the latest dates——“在哪些日子里我们可以预期…发生”。expect sth to do 是固定结构，译“预期/预计某事发生”。考生易把 when 看成时间状语，导致定语从句这层修饰丢失。"}]},{"n":44,"en":"But that, Pearson points out, is only the start of man-machine integration: \"It will be the beginning of the long process of integration that will ultimately lead to a fully electronic human before the end of the next century.\"","refZh":"但 Pearson 指出，这一切仅仅是人机融合的开端：“这将是一段漫长融合进程的开始，而这一进程最终将于下个世纪末之前催生出一种完全电子化的人类。”","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"But that,","lit":"但是，这（一切）","role":"（主干主语（that 为指代词））","note":"难点： that 跨句回指脑机接口突破 本句 that 不指本句任何词，而是回指上一段 Pearson 那段引语——“通过直接连接神经系统，计算机可以感知我们的感受，开发出全感官环境”这一脑机接口突破，参 By linking directly to our nervous system, computers could pick up what we feel。汉译时不能含糊地说“那个”，要还原为“这一切/这种突破/这一进展”才能让读者明白指代对象。"},{"en":"Pearson points out,","lit":"Pearson 指出","role":"（插入语（作者引述））","note":"难点： 插入语提到句首译 Pearson points out 是插入语，英文置于主语与谓语之间打断句子节奏，汉语不接受这样的打断。固定办法是把插入语提到整句开头译“Pearson 指出，…”，让主干 that is only the start 顺下来。"},{"en":"is only the start of man-machine integration:","lit":"仅仅是人机融合的开端：","role":"（主干谓语 + 表语 + 冒号引出引语）","note":"难点： only 译“仅仅/只是”，integration 统一译“人机融合” only 提示作者态度——这只是“开端”而非终点，要把这层“起步阶段”的语气译出。man-machine integration 是全文核心术语（详见第 5 段两次出现），统一译“人机融合/人机一体化”，与下一块的 integration 保持一致。"},{"en":"\"It will be the beginning of the long process of integration","lit":"“这将是这一漫长融合进程的开端","role":"（Pearson 引语主干（it=主语，will be=系动词，beginning=表语）+ of 短语作定语）","note":"难点： It 回指上文 that 同一所指；beginning 与 start 同义复指 引语里的 It 与句首 that 指代同一对象——脑机接口这一突破。beginning 与上文 start 同义，作者用两个词强调“这只是个开始”。the long process of integration 译“漫长的融合进程”，把 long 这一时间跨度的强调译出。"},{"en":"that will ultimately lead to a fully electronic human","lit":"（这一进程）最终将催生一种完全电子化的人类","role":"（that 引导定语从句修饰 process）","note":"难点： ultimately 译“最终”，fully electronic human 是关键科幻词 ultimately 强调时间链条的终点，必须译出“最终/终将”。lead to 译“导致/催生/带来”，不可漏。fully electronic human 字面“完全电子化的人类”，是本文标志性的未来概念，保留字面即可，但 fully 这一“完全”不可省——它对应 partly/half 的反义，体现 Pearson 预测的彻底程度。"},{"en":"before the end of the next century.\"","lit":"在下个世纪结束之前","role":"（时间状语）","note":"难点： next century 取相对值，2001 年文写的是 21 世纪末 the next century 在本文（2001 年原题）语境下指 21 世纪（即 2100 年前）。考生只需译“下个世纪”或“下世纪末”，与原文 next 对应。before the end of 译“在…结束之前/到…末之前”。"}]},{"n":45,"en":"And home appliances will also become so smart that controlling and operating them will result in the breakout of a new psychological disorder—kitchen rage.","refZh":"并且，家用电器也将变得如此智能，以至于操控它们将会导致一种新的心理疾病的爆发——厨房狂躁症。","analysis":"","chunks":[{"en":"And home appliances will also become so smart","lit":"并且家用电器也将变得如此智能","role":"（主干（主语 + 系动词 + 表语）+ so…that 结构的前半）","note":"难点： smart 译“智能”，呼应全文科技语境 smart 在本文科技语境下不是“聪明/机灵”，而是“智能（化）”，对应 smart phone、smart home 同一用法。And 与 also 提示这是上文“技术进步引发社会问题”链条的延续，对应 But he does expect social problems as a result of technological advances，承上启下。"},{"en":"that controlling and operating them","lit":"以至于控制和操作它们（这些家电）","role":"（so…that 的 that 引导结果状语从句；动名词短语作主语，them 回指 home appliances）","note":"难点： so…that 译“如此…以至于”，them 回指家电 so smart that… 是 so…that… 结果状语从句，固定译“如此…以至于…”，不能丢掉这层“因果/程度+结果”关系。controlling and operating 是动名词短语作主语，them 回指本句开头的 home appliances，翻译时可还原为“控制和操作（这些家电）”使语义清晰。"},{"en":"will result in the breakout of a new psychological disorder—kitchen rage.","lit":"将导致一种新的心理疾病的爆发——厨房狂躁症","role":"（结果从句的谓语 + 宾语 + 破折号引出的同位语）","note":"难点： result in 译“导致”、breakout 译“爆发”、kitchen rage 类比 road rage result in 是固定短语，译“导致/引起/造成”，不要拆开。breakout 是 break out 的名词形式，原义“爆发、突然出现”。psychological disorder 是医学术语，译“心理疾病/心理失调/心理障碍”，不可意译成“心理问题”，会丢医学色彩。kitchen rage 这种新造词按 road rage（路怒）、air rage（空怒）类比，译“厨房狂躁症/厨房怒症”——这是英美媒体常见的“X + rage”仿造模式，破折号前后保留对应符号。"}]}]},{"id":"section3","kind":"writing","title":"Section III 写作","directions":"46. Directions: Among all the worthy feelings of mankind, love is probably the noblest, but everyone has his/her own understanding of it. There has been a discussion recently on the issue in a newspaper. Write an essay to the newspaper to 1）show your understanding of the symbolic meaning of the picture below. 2）give a specific example, and 3）give your suggestion as to the best way to show love.","prompt":"46. Directions: Among all the worthy feelings of mankind, love is probably the noblest, but everyone has his/her own understanding of it. There has been a discussion recently on the issue in a newspaper. Write an essay to the newspaper to 1）show your understanding of the symbolic meaning of the picture below. 2）give a specific example, and 3）give your suggestion as to the best way to show love.","points":10,"image":{"src":"assets/writing/2001-section3.jpg","alt":"这是一幅黑白漫画，标题是“爱心是一盏灯，在越黑暗的地方越明亮","width":"1161","height":"766","local":"assets/writing/2001-section3.jpg"},"model":{"essay":"The black-and-white drawing before us is simple yet thought-provoking: at its center stands an oil lamp whose wick burns into a small, smiling flame. As the caption suggests, love is like a lamp that shines all the brighter in darker surroundings. In other words, the picture tells us that human love reveals its warmest and most precious light exactly when people are trapped in hardship and gloom. A concrete example may bring this symbolism to life. When a devastating earthquake struck, countless volunteers, most of them complete strangers, rushed to the ruins day and night. They dug for survivors, donated blood and shared their food with those who had lost everything. In that darkest of moments, their selfless care burned like the little flame in the picture, lighting up hope for people in despair. As far as I am concerned, the best way to show love is not grand words but small, sincere actions in daily life. A helping hand to a stranger, a word of comfort to the lonely, or simple company for our aging parents can all become a lamp for someone in the dark. If each of us keeps our own flame burning, the whole world will surely grow warmer and brighter.","translation":"我们眼前这幅黑白画简单却发人深省：画面中央立着一盏油灯，灯芯燃着一簇微笑的小火苗。正如标题所示，爱就像一盏灯，周遭越黑暗，它照得越明亮。换言之，这幅画告诉我们：正当人们被困于苦难与阴郁之中时，人间的爱恰恰迸发出最温暖、最珍贵的光。\n一个具体的例子能让这层象征鲜活起来。当一场毁灭性的地震来袭，无数志愿者——他们大多素不相识——昼夜奔赴废墟。他们挖掘幸存者、献血，把自己的食物分给一无所有的人。在那最黑暗的时刻，他们无私的关爱如同画中那簇小火苗，为绝望中的人点亮了希望。\n在我看来，表达爱的最佳方式不是豪言壮语，而是日常生活中真诚的小举动。向陌生人伸出的一只援手、对孤独者的一句安慰、给年迈父母的一份简单陪伴，都能成为黑暗中某个人的一盏灯。只要我们每个人都守护好自己心里那簇火苗，整个世界必将变得更加温暖、更加明亮。","breakdown":[{"tag":"【第 1 段】","core":"先白描后点破，寓意到位","text":"【第 1 段】 先白描后点破，寓意到位 。首段前一句 The black-and-white drawing before us is simple yet thought-provoking… 客观白描油灯与微笑火苗，落实「先客观描述」；后用 As the caption suggests, love is like a lamp… 把物象翻成道理，完成 show your understanding of the symbolic meaning of the picture below，兼顾描述与寓意两步。"},{"tag":"【第 2 段】","core":"细节例子对上寓意","text":"【第 2 段】 细节例子对上寓意 。本段以 A concrete example may bring this symbolism to life 过渡，再用地震救援给出 dug for survivors, donated blood and shared their food 等具体动作，最后 burned like the little flame in the picture 一句把例子回扣到画面之光，落实 give a specific example 且不跑题。"},{"tag":"【第 3 段】","core":"对比表态＋日常小事＋升华","text":"【第 3 段】 对比表态＋日常小事＋升华 。末段以 the best way to show love is not grand words but small, sincere actions 用 not…but… 对比亮出主张，列出援手、安慰、陪伴三件可操作小事，再以 the whole world will surely grow warmer and brighter 升华呼应首段的灯光，完成 give your suggestion as to the best way to show love。"}],"wordCount":205}}],"questionCount":40,"objectiveCount":40,"answerTable":{"ans-section1":"完形填空（四选一） Section I （1–20 题） 1 D such as · 2 A tightening · 3 D draft · 4 B illegal · 5 A publicity · 6 C before · 7 D agreed · 8 B offer · 9 B Publication · 10 A storm · 11 B interpretation · 12 C rather than · 13 B makes · 14 A binding · 15 C entitled · 16 A with · 17 D issue · 18 C said · 19 D that · 20 C ensure \n（逐题解析见 完形填空（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-1":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (1) （21–24 题） 21 D · 22 B · 23 A · 24 C \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-2":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (2) （25–28 题） 25 C · 26 A · 27 D · 28 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-3":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (3) （29–32 题） 29 B · 30 D · 31 C · 32 A \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-4":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (4) （33–36 题） 33 C · 34 A · 35 D · 36 B \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-a-5":"阅读理解（四选一） Section II Part A (5) （37–40 题） 37 B · 38 B · 39 C · 40 D \n（逐题解析见 阅读理解（四选一）解析页\n）","ans-section2-part-b":"英译汉（划线句子翻译） Section II Part B \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 英译汉（划线句子翻译）解析页","ans-section3":"写作 Section III \n主观题 · 参考范文与逐题解析见\n 写作解析页"},"coverage":{"objective":40,"explained":40,"missingSections":[]}};
